  "limitations": [
    "Repeated historical contextual1334 dev, not official14326 full dev or new heldout",
    "Native character CTC includes orthographic/context bias, not pure pronunciation or calibrated confidence",
    "Toneless dictionary pronunciation is not waveform-verified; tone/polyphone/same-phone spelling limitations",
    "Phonetic token aggregation changes repeat-collapse semantics and excludes non-Han tokens; exploratory fixed auxiliary",
    "Single-edit same-context whole-utterance CTC marginal avoids reference boundaries but is not an independent local audio judge",
    "Existing float16 cached encoder frames; no hotword bonus in these acoustic scores",
    "Detecting damaging edits is not proof that 9B can use evidence or that end-to-end CER improves",
    "Evidence-score task differs from old correction training; a failure can reflect task/format shift",
    "none changes evidence availability; zero/mismatch have OOD score magnitudes, so comparisons do not prove raw auditory understanding",
    "Both native and predefined phonetic scores included; this is evidence-interface pilot, not isolated-score ablation",
    "Abstention retention is an explicit model decision, not score-threshold recovery; invalid responses are NOT copied from draft",
    "Review edits constructed from previously examined dev predictions; retrospective diagnostic, no new heldout claim",
    "Forced binary selection eliminates free generation failures but also removes explicit abstention; not a same-task accuracy estimate",
    "Autoregressive full target probability combines language/orthography/tokenization with evidence; not acoustic-only confidence",
    "Equal candidate character length does not ensure equal tokenizer length; token-count asymmetry recorded, mean logp diagnostic only",
    "Full-target probability contains downstream context effects; not a pure target-span classifier",
    "Candidate scoring of the same repeated dev is diagnostic; no trained model or unseen test claim",
    "Cross-batch/padding numerical disagreement remains documented in prior audits; all current targets use one fixed unpadded single path",
    "No process-local padding patch is needed or loaded: all attention-mask elements equal one"
  ],
